## Dimensionality Reduction & Feature Selection Portfolio
Overview
This project showcases an end-to-end pipeline for high-dimensional feature selection, model-based dimensionality reduction, and ensemble voting classifiers. Using Scikit-Learn, the workflow evaluates multiple machine learning estimators to isolate the most predictive features while mitigating overfitting and reducing computational complexity.

Key Techniques & Workflow
1. Regularization-Based Selection (LassoCV)
Objective: Automatically tune regularization strength (
𝛼
α) using cross-validation to shrink coefficients of uninformative features to zero.

Implementation: Built a LassoCV regressor on standardized training data (X_train, y_train) to optimize penalty parameters and extract non-zero feature coefficient masks (lcv_mask).

2. Recursive Feature Elimination (RFE)
Objective: Iteratively prune the least important features using tree-based ensemble estimators.

Models Used:

GradientBoostingRegressor

RandomForestRegressor

Configuration: Selected top target features (e.g., reducing 32 features down to 10) by dropping multiple features (step=3) at each iteration.

Mask Generation: Extracted model support vectors (rfe_gb.support_ and rfe_rf.support_ -> gb_mask, rf_mask) to record binary feature importance votes.

3. Ensemble Voting & Meta-Mask Creation
Objective: Combine feature importance votes across disparate models to ensure high-consensus feature selection.

Implementation:

Aggregated votes using NumPy (np.sum([...], axis=0)).

Generated a Meta-Mask requiring unanimous agreement (votes == 3), isolating only the core features agreed upon by all three underlying models.

4. Manual Feature Extraction & Engineering
Objective: Transform raw tabular data into concise, informative features prior to modeling (e.g., deriving unit price from total revenue and quantity sold: sales_df['price'] = sales_df['revenue'] / sales_df['quantity']).

Dimensionality Reduction: Dropped redundant raw features (sales_df.drop([...], axis=1)) to maintain feature independence.

